																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13870617/night-terrors-seeking-idea-critique">Night Terrors - Seeking Idea Critique</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826779">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I have a good idea of what this SCP is, and what she can do, but I need a bit of help figuring out the specifics of her story.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>See, the anomaly isn't that interesting. I feel like there's a lot of &quot;little kids that are dangerous without knowing it&quot; on the wiki and in fiction entirely&#8230; But what <strong>could</strong> set you apart is the story. How you characterize the child, the researchers, and how you create an emotional arc (or journey) for the reader to go on.</p>
<p>Honestly, no one is going to be able to help you write this, its something you have to answer for yourself.</p>
<p>Ask yourself the following questions, and then try to answer them by editing the post to reflect your feelings on the answers:</p>
<ul>
<li>Who's perspective is the article from? Who are we going to relate to as readers?</li>
<li>Where are the stakes for this narrative? Beyond the fact that there are monsters&#8230; what is the intrigue? Only figuring out what is going on with the girl? Is there some way you could up the drama/stakes?</li>
<li>What sort of tone are you going for? Is this scary? Is this an emotional story?</li>
</ul>
<p>Mostly suggest you stay away from vivid descriptions of the abuse the child goes through, unless its super important to the narrative. Shock value is a weak story aspect.</p>

							</div>

								
					
