<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Elevator Pitch</span></p>
<p>So your pitch is some kind of collaboration between all of the major GoIs to stop&#8230; something, however tensions arise due to everyone being suspicious of everyone else? At the moment, this seems more like a Tale than an SCP. It it's also ambitious. Very ambitious. This kind of thing would require an immense amount of research and the like to pull off, and I don't know if a new author such as yourself would be skilled enough to execute this effectively. You're also quite vague about what the GoIs are fighting against. What is it?</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Central Narrative</span></p>
<p>An unknown individual that is notably immature sends a threat message to every GoI, and despite having absolutely no evidence whatsoever to back up their claims, every GoI believes them and unites? This, to a relatively knowledgeable member of the Site (which they probably would be, if, hypothetically, they were reading this) would be an immediate shattering of the suspension of disbelief. This simply isn't feasible. You need to come up with a more pressing threat if you want to make this idea reasonable.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Hook/Attention Grabber</span></p>
<p>That the SCP will unite all of the GoIs, that's a good hook. The next part, which features gratuitous name-dropping of pop culture references (specifically Among Us), isn't. Try to keep away from that if possible.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;don't&nbsp;know&nbsp;about&nbsp;this,&nbsp;buddy</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This idea has the <em>potential</em> to work well, but there are some crippling problems. Firstly, this seems more like a Tale than an SCP (but it could still work as an SCP), due to your vagueness on what the anomaly actually is, and much more of the focus on the 'GoI unification' part. Secondly, your vagueness on the anomaly is really shooting you in the foot here. As I have no idea what the anomaly behind this (and thus the whole point of the article) is, I can't really crit it. What I did see I wasn't impressed by due to logistical problems (see above section for detail). Thirdly, if this is based around Avengers: Infinity War (a mediocre movie, in my opinion), then why write about it if we've already seen it? Wouldn't that be plagiarism and/or boring?<br />
To sum up, I personally don't like this idea due to it being incomplete (what is the anomaly?) and how it is unoriginal (a collaboration between all of the GoIs, if based on Infinity War, isn't original).</p>
<p>I'd recommend two things:<br />
1. Checking out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> (and more specifically <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/cliches-and-you-an-educational-film">this article</a>, first section) for a whole bunch of great essays full of helpful advice!<br />
2. Reaching out to some reviewers from the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a>. They're really helpful and have tonnes of experience!</p>
<p>And finally, to sum up your idea in one sentence<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-615674-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-615674-1')">1</a></sup>:<br />
A mysterious individual contacts every GoI and threatens them with an anomalous object capable of mass destruction, causing the all of the GoIs to unite to find and fight against the individual.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, that's it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!</p>
