<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXXX represents a an extremely damaged and worn down ice dispensing machine. It was originally discovered by a team of Paleontologists on a expedition within the Bone Valley Formation, Florida, United States in 2018. From here it was reported in scientific literature, and was then taken to the foundation. From here it was kept within a anomalous item storage locker until SCP-XXXX began excreting a dark blue gas from its front.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> This gas designated SCP-XXXX-1 is not immediately dangerous, however once this gas is mixed with Oxygen, it will begin turning the surrounding air cold. Small doses of SCP-XXXX-1 is not harmful however large doses make the surrounding area extremely cold and as a consequence can cause frostbite as well as hyperthermia. Because of SCP-XXXX-1 the foundation wanted to look in the exterior of SCP-XXXX to see how it was producing SCP-XXXX-1 on an almost infinite level. However when looking inside of SCP-XXXX they discovered a small metal box witch contained two written notes.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> These notes were signed by Dr. [INSERT NAME HERE] as well having the dates on them, which were months ahead of the current date. The first of these was a copy of an updated page of SCP-XXXX with a stick it note saying &quot;Might come in handy&quot;. The second is a warning stating how the author of the note Dr. [INSERT NAME HERE] is concerned about the foundation accessing the core of SCP-XXXX due to the possibility that SCP-XXXX-1 could flow infinitely out of SCP-XXXX leaving the audience on a cliffhanger.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong>So the first part of the page will just be the usual Special containment procedures, description as well as an added discovery page. Next will be a warning stating only level 4 and over clearance is needed to access, once readers access they will learn about how it was originally kept in a items locker, SCP-XXXX-1 as well as the notes.</p>

